## Overall Risk Assessment

Based on direct inspection of the connected Salesforce org's synced metadata, **none of the custom objects, Apex classes, or permission sets referenced by this project (SLO_Sellout_Report__c, SLO_Sellout_Item__c, Invoice__c, Invoice_Line_Item__c, SLO_SelloutImportController, SLO_SelloutAccountMatcher, etc.) currently exist in the org's tracked metadata**, and the "Potentially Affected Org Components" and "Existing Org Automation" lookups both returned empty. The org's only active trigger (`WRM_RollingForecastTrigger`) fires on an unrelated object (`WRM_RollingForecast__c`), and no flows, other triggers, or permission sets reference Account, Invoice__c, or any SLO_* object in a way that overlaps this project's automation. **Overall deployment risk is Low**: this appears to be a net-new (or first-sync) deployment of the Sellout LWC feature set into this org, with no pre-existing automation to conflict with and no verified downstream consumers of the modified components. The main residual risks are internal to the feature itself (self-consistency of the modified Apex/metadata) rather than collisions with existing org configuration.

